One good session of alchemy takes about six dips plus the quaffing -
much less than a minute of player time - then you can get on with killing
stuff.  Polypiling, on the other hand, *is* quite player-time-consuming
without much excitement, especially since the DevTeam decided that 
non-magic items should almost never turn into magic items, which is why
I generally only do it to rings, and spellbooks, if my wizard starts
with a /Poly), and tools if I happen to have a wand of polymorph and a
glut of unicorn horns.
